# How long each layer's demand survives going unanswered, or the typed reason nobody knows. One row
# per layer: the span a queued order stays an order.
#
# The demand's side of time
#   `pm:Divisibility` sits on `Nameplate`, so `window` is when the supply is there. How long demand
#   lasts is a fact about the demand, and `pm:Demand/patience` is where it is filed; this relation
#   is what makes it possible to ask.
#
# A patience is not a time slack
#   The units tell them apart. A slack is quoted in the unit of the shares it bounds
#   (`slack_unit_mismatch` requires it), and a patience is a span of time that bounds no shares.
#   `merge-holding-composition`'s `shift-line` files both, and they carry the same numbers in
#   different units, because that layer's unit is service time, so the wait and the queue ahead of
#   you are one quantity. The document explains exactly that in a comment. It is a fact about that
#   layer, not a licence to merge the two.
#
# The range and its licence are two relations
#   A shop knows the impatient customer leaves at three minutes and the last at ten; that is the
#   claim. "Service within five minutes" is a negotiated edge on it, and `boundOrigin` is where an
#   edge says whose it is. Reading the two together is the difference between renegotiating a term
#   and measuring again. The edge's owner is the patience claim's own, in epistemics/claims.sqlc
#   where `owns` is `pm:demand/pm:patience`, beside every other claim's.
#
# Zero patience is a claim of zero
#   Never `absent/reason = none`. Demand that leaves the moment it is not served has a patience of
#   zero, and a measured zero is a claim: `patience` is a `pm:StatedClaim`, whose blank arm carries
#   `pm:ClaimAbsenceReason`, and that type has no `none`. So `patience_absent` holds two reasons,
#   never `none`. The validator refuses `none`, and `a_patience_absence_has_no_none` refuses it
#   again on the way in.
#
# What the element is for
#   `merge-group-composition`'s `on-call` layer "does not survive being held", and without a
#   patience element that fact would have nowhere to go but the time slack's
#   `absent/reason = none`, which is a different claim. It is a `timeSlack` of 0, 0 and 0 and a
#   patience beside it. Its patience is `unmeasured`, and the gap between the two is worth a query:
#   a slack of zero is a buffer nobody funded, and a patience of zero is demand that would not use
#   one even if somebody did.
-- pm:Demand/pm:patience, beside the demand it qualifies.
SELECT l.filing, l.layer,
       l.patience_low, l.patience_mode, l.patience_high, l.patience_unit,
       l.patience_absent,
       l.demand_unit
FROM pm.layer l
